config SDXI_VFIO_PCI
	tristate "VFIO support for SDXI PCI devices"
	depends on PCI && PCI_MSI
	depends on SDXI
	select VFIO_PCI_CORE
	help
	  VFIO driver for AMD SDXI (Smart Data Accelerator Interface)
	  PCI devices with savevm/loadvm migration support.

	  The driver saves and restores the small set of writable BAR0
	  control registers (CTL0, CTL2, CXT_L2, RKEY, ERR_CFG, ERR_CTL,
	  ERR_WRT, ERR_RD). Context tables, descriptor rings, and
	  completion-status blocks live in guest RAM and are captured
	  as part of the VM memory snapshot.

	  After resume, the variant driver asks the host SDXI PF driver
	  to restart the VF's contexts so the guest can resume DMA
	  without explicit cooperation.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here; the module
	  will be called sdxi-vfio-pci.
